<p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" xmlns:p15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2012/main" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr>        <p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/>        <p:cNvGrpSpPr/>        <p:nvPr/>      </p:nvGrpSpPr>      <p:grpSpPr>        <a:xfrm>          <a:off x="0" y="0"/>          <a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/>          <a:chOff x="0" y="0"/>          <a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/>        </a:xfrm>      </p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="200" name="PlaceHolder 1"></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="685800" y="1143000"/><a:ext cx="5486040" cy="3085920"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:ln w="0"><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="201" name="PlaceHolder 2"></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="685800" y="4400640"/><a:ext cx="5486040" cy="3600000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln w="0"><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr lIns="91440" tIns="45720" rIns="91440" bIns="45720" anchor="t"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>EF Core&apos;s preview changes concentrate on query translation, modeling, migrations, and provider behavior. Preview 5 introduced an analyzer warning when asynchronous EF queries execute synchronously, helping teams detect a subtle scalability problem. It also changed SQL Server 2022 compatibility to the default and continued work on cleaner generated SQL. Preview 6 added keys and indexes across complex-type properties, unconstrained foreign-key relationships, Cosmos provider improvements, and migration refinements. Preview 7 continued translation and migration work and added Half support for SQLite. MAUI followed a different path, emphasizing reliability and platform capabilities. Across the previews, Microsoft highlighted Windows Maps, cancellation-aware animation overloads, CollectionView2 on Windows, AOT-safe HybridWebView, cross-platform passkey authentication, XAML Incremental Hot Reload, shell route templates, and AOT-safe RelativeSource bindings. Application teams should select the slice relevant to their stack rather than evaluate the whole platform. Data teams can test generated SQL and migrations; mobile teams can focus on platform behavior, build modes, and authentication flows.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>Sources:</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>https://devblogs.microsoft.com/dotnet/dotnet-11-preview-5/</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>https://devblogs.microsoft.com/dotnet/dotnet-11-preview-6/</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>https://devblogs.microsoft.com/dotnet/dotnet-11-preview-7/</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>&lt;number&gt;</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="202" name="PlaceHolder 3"></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" idx="21"/></p:nvPr></p:nvS